{"ts": 1784305912.3081098, "event": "finish", "summary": "Never exited \u2014 held through the full 45-frame window. The trade round-tripped a wide chop band (-15 to +10) for the first ~20 minutes with no clean directional signal (ER10 near 0), then broke into a sustained favorable leg after t=27m, printing a new high almost every few frames (peak intrabar touch ~+38.75, closing near +26.5 at window end). Exit signals (KMDR/PROPP/CLIMAX-against) fired repeatedly during pullbacks off local highs, but each was followed by a recovery to a new high, so none warranted cutting a working winner given giveback stayed well within normal noise. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that fails to make a new high after 2-3 consecutive against-fires (a real momentum stall) rather than treating every dip as noise, since I never got confirmation to actually test an exit rule here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 46}
